  "description": "A dynaset over Dr (ORDER BY ID, fields ID and Vt) is positioned on row 8 (MoveFirst, Move 7) and ID, Vt and Bookmark are read; then Execute deletes ID 8 and Execute inserts ID 8 again with the same values; then ID, Vt and Bookmark are read from the held cursor, MoveNext, MovePrevious, Requery and MoveFirst plus Move 7 each read again. Asks what the held cursor and bookmark show after the row was deleted and its key reinserted. Dr: 20 small rows (ID Long key, A Long, Vt Text(60) 'original text of row <ID>'), ID 1..20. Images: 'before' (the fixture copy as given), then one kept image of the closed file after each step; every step opens the database read/write, makes one mutation and closes it, with the DBEngine still alive.",
